secondary reporting were reviewed.\n- **Time window:** The 16 October to 15 November 2026 window has no confirmed coverage.\n\n## Recommended Preparation Before 17 November\n\nBefore the meeting, the following primary sources should be checked directly for items dated 16 October to 15 November 2026:\n\n- Razorpay's official website and newsroom: [Razorpay](https://razorpay.com) [1]\n- Reserve Bank of India press releases, for any payment aggregator or payments regulation updates: [Reserve Bank of India](https://www.rbi.org.in) [2]\n- Razorpay executive profiles and posts on LinkedIn, for leadership changes\n\nEach item found in these sources should be logged with its date and URL before it is used in the meeting.\n\n## Three Open Questions for the Meeting\n\nBecause no sourced findings were retrieved, these questions are based on the four categories in the brief rather than on confirmed developments. They are intended to surface recent changes directly from Razorpay.\n\n1. Which product launches, feature releases, or pricing changes has Razorpay made in the past month across its India and international operations, and which of them are most relevant to our discussion?\n2. Have any regulatory developments, such as payment aggregator requirements or compliance changes in India or other markets, affected Razorpay's product or partnership plans in recent weeks?\n3. Have there been any recent partnership, funding, or senior leadership changes that would affect who we should work with on this topic going forward?\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] Razorpay (official website, to be reviewed for window-dated items): https://razorpay.com\n[2] Reserve Bank of India (official press releases, to be reviewed for window-dated items): https://www.rbi.org.in",
